NAME
       init - process 1, the ancestor of all processes

SYNOPSIS
       init

DESCRIPTION
       init is the first program the kernel starts and runs as process 1.
       It brings up user space and keeps it running.

       init performs the following:

         o  spawns a single getty(1) on the console;
         o  waits for and reaps child processes, adopting orphans;
         o  respawns getty whenever its login session ends, so the login
            prompt always returns; and
         o  handles shutdown and reboot signals.

       The root filesystem is expected to be mounted already (the kernel
       mounts the USB root at boot); mounting additional filesystems from
       user space is a future addition.

SIGNALS
       SIGTERM   power the machine off
       SIGINT    reboot the machine (Ctrl-Alt-Del)

SEE ALSO
       getty(1), login(1), reboot(1)

AUTHORS
